{
  "version": "1.6.1",
  "changelog": "Two fixes. (1) Download-on-open could never finish: zone building files over 1 MB (riverdale, southfulton and others) come back EMPTY from GitHub's file API, and the editor tried to load the empty reply. Large files are now fetched through GitHub's blob API by their fingerprint, every file downloads on its own fresh connection with retries on network errors, and a failure now shows the real reason (which file, and GitHub's own message) instead of only 'check your connection'. Verified live from a clean machine state with no key: all 7 zones, 166,444 buildings. (2) Packaging: the 1.6.0 installer was built with restrictive file permissions (launcher 'permission denied', invisible menu entry); rebuilt with standard permissions (folders 755, files 644, launcher 755, owner root) plus a build-time permissions check so it cannot ship that way again.",
